<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 342 0 R
  /Alt (This map displays a false-color satellite image of a landscape characterized by dense vegetation and wetland features, overlaid with vector boundaries. The background imagery shows healthy vegetation in bright red tones, interspersed with lighter cyan areas, which likely represent less dense vegetation, bare ground, or water-influenced terrain. Prominent bright cyan polygons with black outlines are labelled 'Corridor feature' in the legend; one is located centrally, and another, larger one representing a river or extensive water body, is visible at the top right. Irregular yellow lines, labelled 'Area boundary,' delineate various polygons across the map, often following land cover transitions. A smaller blue feature, likely a small water body, is also visible within a lighter cyan patch towards the top left. The map includes a scale bar indicating distances of 0, 0.25, 0.5, and 1.0 km, and a North arrow. The imagery is consistent with a Sentinel-2 false-color composite, used for land cover mapping within the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS).)
